  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.Ramesh Babu Alias Ramesh vs State Of Ap on 13 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5396 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/A5 seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.148 of 2019 of Badvel Rural Police Station, YSR Kadapa District, registered for the offences under Sections 188, 272, 273 and 328 of IPC and Sections 57, 58 r/w 26, 30 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 05.08.2019 at 10.00 a.m., when the complainant along with his staff proceeded to Karlapalem Main Road, on suspicion, caught the accused and found the banned tobacco products in their possession and hence, seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.89 of 2018 of Karlapalem Police Station, for the offences stated supra.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
